Tuberville was one of six Republican senators to vote against expanding the COVID-19 Hate Crimes Act, which would allow the [[United States Department of Justice|U.S. Justice Department]] to review hate crimes related to [[COVID-19]] and establish an online database.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/04/14/politics/anti-asian-hate-crimes-senate-vote/index.html |title=Senate advances bill to combat surge of anti-Asian hate crimes |publisher=CNN |last=Rogers |first=Alex |date=April 14, 2021 |access-date=April 14, 2021 |archive-date=April 16, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220416022341/https://www.cnn.com/2021/04/14/politics/anti-asian-hate-crimes-senate-vote/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_lists/roll_call_vote_cfm.cfm?congress=117&session=1&vote=00151 |title=On Cloture on the Motion to Proceed (Motion to Invoke Cloture Re: Motion to Proceed to S. 937) |publisher=United States Senate |date=April 14, 2021 |access-date=April 14, 2021 |archive-date=April 14, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414220446/https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_lists/roll_call_vote_cfm.cfm?congress=117&session=1&vote=00151 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Following the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine]], Tuberville claimed that Putin had ordered the invasion because Russia could not feed its people and required Ukrainian farmland. He inaccurately called Russia a [[communist]] country (Russia abandoned communism after the [[collapse of the Soviet Union]]).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Metzger |first=Bryan |title=Sen. Tommy Tuberville says Russia is still a 'communist country' and is invading Ukraine because 'they need more farmland' |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/tommy-tuberville-communist-russia-invading-ukraine-farmland-comments-2022-2 |access-date=December 14, 2025 |website=Business Insider |language=en-US |date=February 24, 2022 |archive-date=December 9, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251209185013/https://www.businessinsider.com/tommy-tuberville-communist-russia-invading-ukraine-farmland-comments-2022-2 |url-status=live }}</ref>
 
In May 2022, Tuberville introduced the Financial Freedom Act of 2022, which would allow for the inclusion of [[cryptocurrency]] in individual retirement accounts.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Financial Freedom Act Proposed in Senate |url=https://www.ascensus.com/news/news-articles/financial-freedom-act-proposed-in-senate/ |access-date=May 11, 2022 |website=Ascensus LLC |language=en |archive-date=May 17, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220517141355/https://www.ascensus.com/news/news-articles/financial-freedom-act-proposed-in-senate/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Tuberville |first=Tommy |date=May 5, 2022 |title=Op-ed: Cryptocurrency should be allowed in individual retirement plans. That's why I'm introducing the Financial Freedom Act |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/05/05/allow-cryptocurrency-in-individual-retirement-plans-sen-tuberville.html |access-date=May 11, 2022 |website=CNBC |language=en |archive-date=May 13, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220513035147/https://www.cnbc.com/2022/05/05/allow-cryptocurrency-in-individual-retirement-plans-sen-tuberville.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Speaking at a Trump rally in [[Nevada]] on October 8, 2022, Tuberville claimed that Democrats are "pro-crime", "want to take over what you've got", and "want {{Sic|[[Reparations for slavery in the United States|reparation]]}} because they think the people that do the crime are owed that".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Swetlik |first=Sarah |date=October 9, 2022 |title=Tuberville: 'Pro-crime' Democrats want 'reparations' for 'people who do the crime' |url=https://www.al.com/news/2022/10/tuberville-pro-crime-democrats-want-reparations-for-people-who-do-the-crime.html |access-date=October 10, 2022 |website=AL.com |language=en}}</ref> These remarks were widely condemned as inaccurate<ref>{{Cite news |last=Scott |first=Eugene |date=October 10, 2022 |title=Democrats call Sen. Tuberville's comments about crime and reparations racist |newspaper=Washington Post |url=https://taskandpurpose.com/news/army-investigation-pat-donahoe-social-media/}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Bump |first=Philip |date=October 10, 2022 |title=Important to Tuberville's comments on race: He represents Alabama |newspaper=Washington Post |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/10/tuberville-race-trump-rally-alabama-football/}}</ref> and racist;<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nzanga |first=Merdie |title=GOP Sen. Tommy Tuberville promotes racist narrative about Black people, crime at Trump rally |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/10/09/tommy-tuberville-democrats-crime-trump-rally/8229722001/ |access-date=October 10, 2022 |website=USA TODAY |language=en-US |archive-date=October 9, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221009215254/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/10/09/tommy-tuberville-democrats-crime-trump-rally/8229722001/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Schonfeld |first=Zach |date=October 9, 2022 |title=Bakari Sellers: Tuberville can 'go to hell' over reparations remark |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/sunday-talk-shows/3680135-bakari-sellers-tuberville-can-go-to-hell-over-reparation-remark/ |access-date=October 10, 2022 |website=The Hill |language=en-US |archive-date=October 9, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221009232114/https://thehill.com/homenews/sunday-talk-shows/3680135-bakari-sellers-tuberville-can-go-to-hell-over-reparation-remark/ |url-status=live }}</ref> for example, the [[NAACP]] called them "flat out racist, ignorant and utterly sickening".<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 10, 2022 |title=NAACP President Derrick Johnson on Sen. Tuberville's Racist Comments this Weekend {{!}} NAACP |url=https://naacp.org/articles/naacp-president-derrick-johnson-sen-tubervilles-racist-comments-weekend |access-date=October 10, 2022 |website=naacp.org |language=en |archive-date=October 10, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221010183359/https://naacp.org/articles/naacp-president-derrick-johnson-sen-tubervilles-racist-comments-weekend |url-status=live }}</ref>

Tuberville was among the 31 Senate Republicans who voted against final passage of the [[Fiscal Responsibility Act of 2023]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4031302-here-are-the-senators-who-voted-against-the-bill-to-raise-the-debt-ceiling/|title=Here are the senators who voted against the bill to raise the debt ceiling|first=Aris|last=Folley|date=June 1, 2023|access-date=June 17, 2023|work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]|archive-date=June 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230602084725/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4031302-here-are-the-senators-who-voted-against-the-bill-to-raise-the-debt-ceiling/|url-status=live}}</ref> telling reporters, "This bill does not go nearly far enough to reform our broken budget".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/tuberville-britt-vote-no-as-u-s-senate-passes-debt-ceiling-bill|title=Tuberville, Britt vote 'no' as U.S. Senate passes debt ceiling bill|last=Taylor|first=Daniel|work=[[1819 News]]|date=June 2, 2023|access-date=June 2, 2023}}</ref>

In June 2024, Tuberville called Ukrainian president [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]] a "dictator" and said that Russian president [[Vladimir Putin]] "doesn't want Ukraine. He doesn't want Europe. Hell, he's got enough land of his own. He just wants to make sure he doesn't have United States weapons in Ukraine pointing at Moscow."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thornton |first1=William |title=Tommy Tuberville says Putin 'doesn't want' Ukraine: 'He's got enough land of his own' |url=https://www.al.com/news/2024/06/tommy-tuberville-says-putin-doesnt-want-ukraine-hes-got-enough-land-of-his-own.html |access-date=June 7, 2024 |work=[[al.com]] |date=June 6, 2024}}</ref>

In June 2025, Tuberville drew backlash after appearing on [[Benny Johnson (columnist)|Benny Johnson]]'s show, where he called people in urban areas "inner-city rats" who "live off the federal government" and called on President Trump to "send them back home".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Thornton |first=William |date=2025-06-26 |title=Tuberville says 'inner city rats' live off the American taxpayers: Trump should send them 'back home' |url=https://www.al.com/politics/2025/06/tuberville-says-inner-city-rats-live-off-the-american-taxpayers-trump-should-send-them-back-home.html |access-date=2025-06-29 |website=al |language=en}}</ref>

==== Objections to the 2020 U.S. presidential election ====
After taking office in January 2021, Tuberville joined a group of Republican senators who announced they would formally object to counting electoral votes won by Democratic president-elect [[Joe Biden]] in the [[2020 United States presidential election|2020 presidential election]].<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Yourish |first1=Karen |last2=Buchanan |first2=Larry |last3=Lu |first3=Denise |date=January 7, 2021 |title=The 147 Republicans Who Voted to Overturn Election Results |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/01/07/us/elections/electoral-college-biden-objectors.html |access-date=December 14, 2022 |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=January 7, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210107065429/https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/01/07/us/elections/electoral-college-biden-objectors.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The objections were part of a continued effort by Trump and his allies to [[Attempts to overturn the 2020 United States presidential election|overturn his defeat in the election]].

When the [[2021 United States Electoral College vote count|Electoral College count]] was held on January 6, [[pro-Trump]] rioters [[2021 storming of the United States Capitol|stormed the Capitol]], forcing officials to evacuate their chambers before the count was completed. Trump contacted Tuberville during the riot through the cell phone of Utah senator [[Mike Lee]], whom Trump misdialed.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Romboy|first=Dennis|date=January 7, 2021|title=How President Trump misdialed Utah Sen. Mike Lee while the Capitol was under siege|url=https://www.deseret.com/utah/2021/1/7/22218897/donald-trump-mike-lee-misdial-capitol-siege-congress-electoral-insurrection-moore-curtis-stewart|access-date=January 8, 2021|website=Deseret News|language=en|archive-date=January 10, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210110010521/https://www.deseret.com/utah/2021/1/7/22218897/donald-trump-mike-lee-misdial-capitol-siege-congress-electoral-insurrection-moore-curtis-stewart|url-status=live}}</ref> The count resumed that evening once the Capitol was secured.

Tuberville voted in support of an objection to Arizona's electoral votes and an objection to Pennsylvania's electoral votes, which were both won by Biden. He was one of six Republican senators to support the former objection and one of seven to support the latter objection; the remainder of the Senate defeated the objections.<ref>{{cite web|last=Durkee|first=Alison|date=January 6, 2021|title=Congress Approves Arizona's Electoral Votes Following GOP Objections, Capitol Siege|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2021/01/06/congress-approves-arizonas-electoral-votes-following-gop-objections-capitol-siege/?sh=317276613375|access-date=January 6, 2021|website=Forbes|archive-date=January 9, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210109060222/https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2021/01/06/congress-approves-arizonas-electoral-votes-following-gop-objections-capitol-siege/?sh=317276613375|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=January 7, 2021|title=Roll Call Vote 117th Congress - 1st Session|url=https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_lists/vote_menu_117_1.htm|access-date=January 7, 2021|website=USSen|language=en-US|quote=A group of Republican lawmakers led by Sen. Ted Cruz (R-Texas) and Rep. Paul Gosar (R-Ariz.) objected to Arizona's electoral votes Wednesday afternoon, prompting up to two hours of debate before both chambers of Congress voted on whether to accept the results.|agency=U.S. Senate|archive-date=January 9, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210109011305/https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_lists/vote_menu_117_1.htm|url-status=live}}</ref> No further objections to the electoral votes were debated and the count concluded on the morning of January 7, certifying Biden's victory over Trump.

==== 2021 storming of the United States Capitol ====
On May 28, 2021, Tuberville voted against creating an independent commission to investigate the [[January 6 United States Capitol attack|2021 United States Capitol attack]].<ref>{{cite news |newspaper=Washington Post |date=May 28, 2021 |title=Which senators supported a Jan. 6 Capitol riot commission |first1=Peter W. |last1=Stevenson |first2=Adrian |last2=Blanco |first3=Daniela |last3=Santamariña |access-date=November 7, 2023 |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/interactive/2021/january6-commission-senators-vote/ |archive-date=May 26, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210526225939/https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/interactive/2021/january6-commission-senators-vote/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In January 2025, after Trump [[pardon of January 6 United States Capitol attack defendants|pardoned January 6 United States Capitol attack defendants]] on the first day of [[Second presidency of Donald Trump|his second presidency]], Tuberville told [[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] he fully supported the pardons. Asked about pardons for rioters who attacked police, Tuberville said: "I don't believe it because I didn't see it."<ref>{{cite news|last1=Scott|first1=Rachel|last2=Murray|first2=Isabella|last3=Ibssa|first3=Lalee|last4=Pecorin|first4=Allison|date=January 21, 2025|url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/senate-republicans-mixed-reactions-trumps-pardons-jan-6/story?id=117948067|title=Senate Republicans have mixed reactions to Trump's pardons for Jan. 6 violent offenders|publisher=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|access-date=January 6, 2026|archive-date=January 8, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260108200117/https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/senate-republicans-mixed-reactions-trumps-pardons-jan-6/story?id=117948067|url-status=live}}</ref>

====''Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization''====
When ''[[Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization]]'' came before the Supreme Court in 2022, Tuberville signed an [[Amicus curiae|amicus brief]] supporting the overturning of ''[[Roe v. Wade]]'' and its federal protection of abortion. After ''Roe v. Wade'' was overturned in June 2022, Tuberville called it a "victory for life".<ref>{{cite press release |title=Tuberville Statement on Supreme Court's Final Opinion in Dobbs Case |via=senate.gov |url=https://www.tuberville.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/tuberville-statement-on-supreme-courts-final-opinion-in-dobbs-case/ |access-date=June 24, 2022 |website=Coach Tommy Tuberville |archive-date=June 24, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220624152311/https://www.tuberville.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/tuberville-statement-on-supreme-courts-final-opinion-in-dobbs-case/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==== Same-sex marriage ====
In 2022, Tuberville responded to a question about the [[Respect for Marriage Act]], which would federally codify [[same-sex marriage]], by saying there was "no need for legislating on gay marriage". He also said, "I'm all about live life the way you want to. It's a free country."<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 21, 2022 |title=Shelby, Tuberville issue statements on bill to codify marriage equality |url=https://whnt.com/news/politics/shelby-tuberville-issue-statements-on-bill-to-codify-marriage-equality/ |access-date=December 14, 2022 |website=WHNT.com |first=Zach |last=Hester |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220721012421/https://whnt.com/news/politics/shelby-tuberville-issue-statements-on-bill-to-codify-marriage-equality/ |archive-date=2022-07-21 |url-status=live |language=en-US}}</ref> He voted against the bill,<ref>{{Cite news |last=Karni |first=Annie |date=December 13, 2022 |title=The 12 Republican Senators Who Voted for the Same-Sex Marriage Law |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/12/13/us/politics/republican-senators-vote-same-sex-marriage.html |access-date=December 14, 2022 |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=December 14, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221214014351/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/12/13/us/politics/republican-senators-vote-same-sex-marriage.html |url-status=live }}</ref> which passed and was signed into law.

==== Stock trading ====

Tuberville failed to timely disclose approximately 132 stock trades made between January and May 2021 that violated the [[STOCK Act]].<ref name="Seddiq">{{Cite web |last=Seddiq |first=Oma |title=Sen.Tommy Tuberville, who violated stock-trading rules 132 times last year, says it's 'ridiculous' to ban lawmakers from trading stocks |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/tommy-tuberville-ridiculous-to-ban-lawmakers-from-trading-stocks-2022-2 |access-date=February 10, 2022 |website=Business Insider |language=en-US |date=February 9, 2022 |archive-date=February 11, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220211181233/https://www.businessinsider.com/tommy-tuberville-ridiculous-to-ban-lawmakers-from-trading-stocks-2022-2 |url-status=live }}</ref> These transactions, valued between $894,000 and $3.56 million, were not reported to the Senate until several months after the legal deadline. He was found to have bought or sold stocks and options in 17 companies that had business before Senate committees on which he served, such as the [[United States Senate Committee on Armed Services|Armed Services Committee]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Kelly |first1=Kate |last2=Playford |first2=Adam |last3=Parlapiano |first3=Alicia |title= Stock Trades Reported by Nearly a Fifth of Congress Show Possible Conflicts |url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/13/us/politics/congress-stock-trading-investigation.html |access-date=April 4, 2026 |website=New York Times |language=en-US |date=September 13, 2022 }}</ref>

In 2022, Tuberville dismissed proposals to ban lawmakers from trading stocks as "ridiculous".<ref name="Seddiq"/>

==== Islam ====

In 2025, Tuberville and Senator [[John Cornyn]] introduced the "No Sharia" Act, which would prohibit the implementation of [[sharia]], or [[Islamic]] law. On the Senate floor, Tuberville said, "Radical Islamists would like to see every freedom-loving American dead. This isn't politically correct to say, but it's true. If you live in America and practice sharia law, you should be deported immediately."<ref name="Darrington">{{Cite web|last=Darrington|first=Patrick|date=October 9, 2025|title=Tuberville call to ban 'sharia law' shows 'dangerous hatred against American Muslims,' advocate says|url=https://www.al.com/politics/2025/10/tuberville-call-to-ban-sharia-law-shows-dangerous-hatred-against-american-muslims-advocate-says.html|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=AL.com|language=en|archive-date=December 2, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251202020651/https://www.al.com/politics/2025/10/tuberville-call-to-ban-sharia-law-shows-dangerous-hatred-against-american-muslims-advocate-says.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Knight|first=Jerrod|date=October 16, 2025|title=Cornyn, Tuberville file 'No Sharia Act,' calling for ban already in place|url=https://www.ketr.org/news/2025-10-16/cornyn-tuberville-file-no-sharia-act-calling-for-ban-already-in-place|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=[[KETR]]|language=en|archive-date=December 31, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251231014738/https://www.ketr.org/news/2025-10-16/cornyn-tuberville-file-no-sharia-act-calling-for-ban-already-in-place|url-status=live}}</ref> He added that Muslim immigrants in Europe have "taken over France, Italy, the UK. That's been a process. Now they have all mayors from these from these Islamic countries, and so they're trying to change into sharia law [...] Wake up, America. They're here, they're on our shores, and they're trying to change our way of life."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Poor|first=Jeff|date=November 3, 2025|title='Wake up, America. They're here, they're on our shores': Tuberville warns of Islamic influx, Sharia law|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/wake-up-america-theyre-here-theyre-on-our-shores-tuberville-warns-of-islamic-influx-sharia-law|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=[[1819 News]]|language=en|archive-date=December 20, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251220160226/https://1819news.com/news/item/wake-up-america-theyre-here-theyre-on-our-shores-tuberville-warns-of-islamic-influx-sharia-law|url-status=live}}</ref> After the [[2025 Washington, D.C., National Guard shooting]], allegedly perpetrated by an Afghan immigrant, Tuberville called for a [[Muslim immigration ban|ban on Muslim immigration]], writing on X: "We must IMMEDIATELY BAN all ISLAM immigrants and DEPORT every single Islamist who is living among us just waiting to attack."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Mancini|first=Ryan|date=November 27, 2025|title=GOP senator calls to ban, deport 'Islam' immigrants over National Guard shooting|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5624742-tuberville-calls-ban-islamic-immigrants/#:~:text=GOP%20senator%20calls%20to%20ban,during%20its%2020%2Dyear%20war.|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=The Hill|language=en|archive-date=December 4, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251204085946/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5624742-tuberville-calls-ban-islamic-immigrants/#:~:text=GOP%20senator%20calls%20to%20ban,during%20its%2020%2Dyear%20war.|url-status=live}}</ref>

Tuberville has called Islam a "cult" that is "incompatible with western values", telling an [[Infowars]] reporter, "Muslim communities are moving everywhere. In every state, they're building mosques, they're having these five prayers a day, they're pushing this cult on everybody across this country." Tuberville spoke out against the proposed move of the Islamic Academy of Alabama to [[Hoover, Alabama]], saying, "If you believe in the [[Quran]] and go by sharia law and want to chant '[[Death to America]]' and teach that nonsense in these schools, I don't want you here [...] Muslims go by the Quran. And the Quran is cited on the Islamic Academy of Alabama's website. The Quran says to kill all infidels. That means all people who don't believe in Islam." The academy's [[assistant principal]] denied that the school promoted sharia law or any political ideology. After the academy decided not to relocate, Tuberville said, "This week, the people of Hoover, Alabama, came together and sent a clear message. We do not want extremist Islamic indoctrination centers taking over our state [...] We're at war in this country with all the people that have come here from all over the world. And listen, we love immigration. We're...all a part of an immigrant family one time and the other. But a lot of people come here and they want to assimilate. Not the group coming here from the Muslim countries. They have an agenda." Tuberville told [[Steve Bannon]], "Muslim immigrants are bringing World War III to American soil."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bryant |first=Joseph |date=December 7, 2025 |title=Islamic school says Tuberville's 'cult' remarks put students in danger, 'fuel fear, prejudice' |url=https://www.al.com/politics/2025/12/islamic-school-says-tubervilles-cult-remarks-put-students-in-danger-fuel-fear-prejudice.html |access-date=December 14, 2025 |website=AL.com |language=en |archive-date=December 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251217160756/https://www.al.com/politics/2025/12/islamic-school-says-tubervilles-cult-remarks-put-students-in-danger-fuel-fear-prejudice.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Conlon |first=Riley |date=December 12, 2025 |title='Incompatible with our Western values': Sen. Tuberville doubles down on Islamic Academy of Alabama |url=https://www.wvtm13.com/article/alabama-islamic-academy-tommy-tuberville-hoover/69702684 |access-date=December 14, 2025 |website=[[WVTM-TV]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Gann|first=Heather|date=December 9, 2025|title=Tuberville celebrates Islamic school abandoning Hoover move: 'Muslim immigrants are bringing WWIII' |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/tuberville-celebrates-islamic-school-abandoning-170801212.html|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=AL.com|language=en}}</ref>

On the [[Alex Jones]] show, Tuberville accused members of Congress of supporting [[Hamas]]. The [[Council on American-Islamic Relations]] has accused Tuberville of fostering [[Islamophobia|anti-Muslim bigotry]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Phillips|first=Chance|date=October 20, 2025|title=Sen. Tuberville's anti-Sharia bills are "bigotry" and "unconstitutional," CAIR says|url=https://www.alreporter.com/2025/10/20/sen-tubervilles-anti-sharia-bills-are-bigotry-and-unconstitutional-cair-says/|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=Alabama Political Reporter|language=en}}</ref> After [[Zohran Mamdani]], a Muslim, was elected mayor of New York City, Tuberville said, "We lost New York. It will be completely Muslim in three or four years."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Niemitz|first=Brian|date=November 7, 2025|title=Alabama senator claims NYC will be 'completely Muslim in 3-4 years'|url=https://www.nydailynews.com/2025/11/07/alabama-senator-tommy-tuberville-predicts-muslims-takeover-new-york-city/|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=[[New York Daily News]]|language=en|archive-date=December 2, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251202072045/https://www.nydailynews.com/2025/11/07/alabama-senator-tommy-tuberville-predicts-muslims-takeover-new-york-city/|url-status=live}}</ref> Of Mamdani, who was born in [[Uganda]], Tuberville said, "I think we ought to pack him up and send him home."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Taylor|first=Daniel|date=October 21, 2025|title=Tuberville on probable future Muslim mayor of New York: 'Pack him up and send him home'|url=https://1819news.com/news/item/tuberville-on-probable-future-muslim-mayor-of-new-york-pack-him-up-and-send-him-home|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=1819 News|language=en|archive-date=January 3, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260103024015/https://1819news.com/news/item/tuberville-on-probable-future-muslim-mayor-of-new-york-pack-him-up-and-send-him-home|url-status=live}}</ref> He has called Mamdani an "openly jihadist terrorist sympathizer" and a "radical Islamist".<ref>{{Cite web|last=Tuberville|first=Tommy|date=October 28, 2025|title=Tuberville: "Radical Islam is Fundamentally Incompatible with our Western Values"|url=https://www.tuberville.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/tuberville-radical-islam-is-fundamentally-incompatible-with-our-western-values/|access-date=December 14, 2025|website=Coach Tommy Tuberville: Senator for Alabama|language=en|archive-date=December 29, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251229155355/https://www.tuberville.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/tuberville-radical-islam-is-fundamentally-incompatible-with-our-western-values/|url-status=live}}</ref> When [[Ghazala Hashmi]] was sworn in as [[Lieutenant Governor of Virginia]] using a [[Quran]], Tuberville wrote, "The enemy is inside the gates."<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cason|first=Mike|date=January 20, 2026|title=Tuberville 'really thinks poorly' of Alabama voters, Hillary Clinton running mate says|url=https://www.al.com/politics/2026/01/tuberville-really-thinks-poorly-of-alabama-voters-hillary-clinton-running-mate-says.html|access-date=January 23, 2026|website=AL.com|language=en}}</ref> In March 2026, Tuberville posted a photo of the [[September 11 attacks]] alongside Mamdani, again writing, "The enemy is inside the gates."<ref>{{cite news|last=Sprunt|first=Barbara|title=House GOP leadership silent as more members post anti-Muslim statements|url=https://www.npr.org/2026/03/14/g-s1-113667/republicans-sharia-law-andy-ogles-mike-johnson|access-date=March 14, 2026|newspaper=NPR|date=March 14, 2026|archive-date=March 14, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260314092349/https://www.npr.org/2026/03/14/g-s1-113667/republicans-sharia-law-andy-ogles-mike-johnson|url-status=live}}</ref>

