==== Veterans ====
In 2022, Tuberville was among the 11 senators who voted against the [[Honoring our PACT Act of 2022]], a bill that provided funding for research and benefits for up to 3.5 million veterans exposed to toxic substances during their service.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nzanga |first=Merdie |title=GOP senators vote against PACT act, a bill to help veterans impacted by toxic substances |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/08/03/pact-act-11-senate-republicans-opposed/10223007002/ |access-date=2025-05-22 |website=USA TODAY |language=en-US |archive-date=May 31, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250531035958/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/08/03/pact-act-11-senate-republicans-opposed/10223007002/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Dress |first=Brad |date=2022-08-03 |title=These 11 GOP senators voted against the Honoring Our Pact Act |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/3586430-these-11-gop-senators-voted-against-the-honoring-our-pact-act/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250505013141/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/3586430-these-11-gop-senators-voted-against-the-honoring-our-pact-act/ |archive-date=2025-05-05 |access-date=2025-05-22 |work=The Hill |language=en-US}}</ref>

==== Transgender policy ====
Tuberville has backed several bills intended to restrict various activities by [[transgender]] people.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Migdon |first1=Brooke |title=GOP lawmakers look to ban transgender athletes from women's sports |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/lgbtq/5072406-gop-lawmakers-look-to-ban-transgender-athletes-from-sports/ |access-date=February 3, 2025 |agency=The Hill |date=January 5, 2025}}</ref>

In February 2023, he co-sponsored a bill to prevent people with a history or diagnosis of [[gender dysphoria]] from serving in the U.S. military, with limited exceptions.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Rubio, Banks Introduce Bill to Regulate Transgender Service in U.S. Military |date=February 16, 2023 |url=https://www.rubio.senate.gov/rubio-banks-introduce-bill-to-regulate-transgender-service-in-u-s-military/ |access-date=April 26, 2023 |publisher=[[Marco Rubio]] |via=senate.gov |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Koplowitz |first=Howard |date=February 17, 2023 |title=Tuberville co-sponsors bill banning trans soldiers |url=https://www.al.com/politics/2023/02/not-the-time-to-socially-experiment-with-our-armed-forces-tuberville-co-sponsors-bill-banning-trans-soldiers.html |access-date=April 26, 2023 |publisher=[[AL.com]] |language=en |archive-date=April 26, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426033319/https://www.al.com/politics/2023/02/not-the-time-to-socially-experiment-with-our-armed-forces-tuberville-co-sponsors-bill-banning-trans-soldiers.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

In March 2023, he reintroduced a bill to forbid public schools from allowing a trans girl or woman to participate in a girl's or women's sport. Co-sponsored by 19 Republicans, the act says gender would be "recognized based solely on a person's reproductive biology and genetics at birth" rather than how a person identifies.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Griesbach |first=Rebecca |date=March 1, 2023 |title=Tuberville again pushes bill to block transgender athletes from women's sports |url=https://www.al.com/educationlab/2023/03/tuberville-again-pushes-bill-to-restrict-transgender-athletes-from-womens-sports.html |access-date=April 26, 2023 |publisher=[[AL.com]] |language=en |archive-date=April 26, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426043043/https://www.al.com/educationlab/2023/03/tuberville-again-pushes-bill-to-restrict-transgender-athletes-from-womens-sports.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

On March 25, 2023, Tuberville complained publicly about a video showing Lieutenant Junior Grade Audrey Knutson, who is nonbinary, reading a poem during a spoken-word event aboard the aircraft carrier {{USS|Gerald R. Ford}}. The video had gone viral after the U.S. Navy posted it to its [[Instagram]] page. After Tuberville told the Senate Armed Services Committee that he had "a lot of problems with the video", Admiral [[Michael M. Gilday|Mike Gilday]], [[Chief of Naval Operations|chief of naval operations]], said he was "particularly proud of this sailor" and added that if someone is "willing to serve and willing to take the same oath that you and I took to put their life on the line, then I'm proud to serve beside them."<ref>{{cite news |last=Liebermann |first=Oren |date=April 18, 2023 |title=Top US Navy admiral defends non-binary sailor amid some Republican criticism |url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/18/politics/gilday-defends-non-binary-sailor/index.html |access-date=April 26, 2023 |work=[[CNN]] |language=en |archive-date=April 26, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426001232/https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/18/politics/gilday-defends-non-binary-sailor/index.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=U.S. Navy JAG Corps on Instagram: "No matter your background, lifestyle, gender, sexuality or religious beliefs, there is a place for you in the Navy. #NavyJAG #usnavy #americasnavy #strongertogether" |url=https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cq6MnU1p5Y0/ |date=April 11, 2023 |access-date=April 26, 2023 |work=[[United States Navy Judge Advocate General's Corps]] |via=[[Instagram]] |language=en |archive-date=April 26, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230426043043/https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cq6MnU1p5Y0/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On March 29, 2024, Tuberville accused the Democratic Party of being a "Satanic cult" in response to a tweet by the [[New York Post]] about the banning of religious-themed designs from the White House Easter Egg art contest. His comment came at a time of widespread backlash by right-wing to far-right politicians and pundits after Biden publicly acknowledged [[International Transgender Day of Visibility]], which fell on the same date as Easter in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benen |first=Steve |date=April 2, 2024 |title=Tommy Tuberville accuses Dems of being part of 'a Satanic cult' |url=https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow-show/maddowblog/tommy-tuberville-accuses-dems-part-satanic-cult-rcna146033 |website=MSNBC |access-date=April 3, 2024 |archive-date=April 3, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240403152858/https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow-show/maddowblog/tommy-tuberville-accuses-dems-part-satanic-cult-rcna146033 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In January 2025, Tuberville said that transgender children should "live in fear" of their parents as he believed the parents were turning them trans, which Tuberville called "child abuse" and an "absolute disgrace". ''[[LGBTQ Nation]]'' refuted these claims, saying that "there is no evidence that a person who is not LGBTQ+ can be turned LGBTQ+ by their parents".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bollinger |first=Alex |date=January 23, 2025 |title=Unhinged GOP senator says trans kids should "live in fear" of their own parents |url=https://www.lgbtqnation.com/2025/01/unhinged-gop-senator-says-trans-kids-should-live-in-fear-of-their-own-parents/ |website=LGBTQ Nation |access-date=January 24, 2025 |archive-date=January 23, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250123170541/https://www.lgbtqnation.com/2025/01/unhinged-gop-senator-says-trans-kids-should-live-in-fear-of-their-own-parents/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On September 23, 2026, Tuberville claimed without evidence that "deranged" transgender people and the [[furry fandom]] were [[Misinformation about violence by transgender people|tied to recent mass shootings]], and that "many" furries (who he said have "a deranged fetish of dressing up like an animal") worked as aircraft pilots and air traffic controllers, while also proposing the reopening of mental institutions and suggesting that those convicted of providing gender-affirming care be incarcerated. Former senator [[Doug Jones (politician)|Doug Jones]] called it the strangest Senate floor speech he had ever heard.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sharp |first=John |date=2026-09-23 |title=Doug Jones: Tuberville's furry pilot Senate floor speech is 'the strangest I have ever heard' |url=https://www.al.com/politics/2026/09/doug-jones-tubervilles-furry-pilot-senate-floor-speech-is-the-strangest-i-have-ever-heard.html |access-date=2026-09-25 |website= [[AL.com]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Smith |first=Ruth Serven |date=2026-09-23 |title= Tuberville calls transgender people 'deranged' on Senate floor: 'Bring back mental institutions' |url= https://www.al.com/politics/2026/09/tuberville-calls-transgender-people-deranged-on-senate-floor-bring-back-mental-institutions.html |access-date=2026-09-25 |website=al |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= Lindahl |first=Jennifer |title=Tuberville makes unfounded claims that airplane staffs are furries |url= https://www.montgomeryadvertiser.com/story/news/politics/elections/2026/09/24/tuberville-alleges-many-airline-workers-are-furries-what-we-know/91917205007/ |access-date=2026-09-25 |website=Montgomery Advertiser |language=en-US}}</ref> Comedian [[Jimmy Kimmel]] satirized the speech on ''[[Jimmy Kimmel Live!]]'' that evening, saying he could not "think of a more serious made-up problem in this country right now than furries flying airplanes".<ref>{{Cite news |title= MAGA Senator Goes on Crazed Posting Spree About Furries |url= https://newrepublic.com/post/215838/maga-senator-tommy-tuberville-furries |access-date=2026-09-25 |work=The New Republic |issn=0028-6583}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Kimmins |first=Leigh |date=2026-09-24 |title= MAGA Senator Roasted Over Bizarre 'Furry' Pilot Freakout |url= https://www.thedailybeast.com/maga-senator-tommy-tuberville-roasted-over-bizarre-furry-pilot-freakout/ |access-date=2026-09-25 |website=The Daily Beast |language=en}}</ref>

==== Hold on military nominations ====
[[File:210610-D-TT977-0181 (51239237105).jpg|thumb|right|Tuberville speaks with U.S. Defense Secretary [[Lloyd Austin]] in June 2021.]]
In December 2022, after Defense Secretary [[Lloyd Austin]] announced an upcoming policy to allow pregnant service members leave and reimbursement of travel costs so that they may obtain legal abortions in the wake of the Supreme Court ruling overturning ''[[Roe v. Wade]]'', Tuberville threatened to put a [[Senate hold]] on all military promotions in protest of the policy.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Shane |first1=Leo |last2=Gould |first2=Joe |title=Senator vows hold on military nominees over Pentagon abortion policy |url=https://www.defensenews.com/pentagon/2022/12/06/senator-vows-hold-on-military-nominees-over-pentagon-abortion-policy/ |access-date=November 2, 2023 |work=[[Defense News]] |date=October 7, 2022}}</ref> The policy was instituted in February 2023, with Tuberville announcing a day later that he would hold all "civilian, flag, and general officer nominations" due to the "illegal expansion of DoD authority and gross misuse of taxpayer dollars" for abortions.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Swetlik |first1=Sarah |title=Tuberville puts hold on defense nominees over policy that will 'facilitate thousands of abortions' |url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/02/tuberville-puts-hold-on-defense-nominees-over-policy-that-will-facilitate-thousands-of-abortions.html |access-date=November 2, 2023 |work=[[al.com]] |date=February 17, 2023 |archive-date=November 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102100823/https://www.al.com/news/2023/02/tuberville-puts-hold-on-defense-nominees-over-policy-that-will-facilitate-thousands-of-abortions.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Over the next few months, Tuberville's hold blocked the filling of hundreds of senior positions. "Without these leaders in place, these holes severely limit the department's ability to ensure the right person is in place at the right time, and to ensure a strategic readiness and operational success", Pentagon deputy press secretary Sabrina Singh said on June 20.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dress |first=Brad |date=2023-06-20 |title=Pentagon slams Tuberville for setting 'dangerous precedent' by holding up nominations |url=https://thehill.com/policy/defense/4058909-pentagon-slams-tuberville-for-setting-dangerous-precedent-by-holding-up-nominations/ |access-date=2023-06-22 |website=The Hill |language=en-US |archive-date=June 22, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230622144233/https://thehill.com/policy/defense/4058909-pentagon-slams-tuberville-for-setting-dangerous-precedent-by-holding-up-nominations/ |url-status=live }}</ref>{{efn|name= tubervilleBlock |1= As of June 16, 2023, blocks have occurred for vacancies on the [[Joint Chiefs of Staff]]<ref name= jcsBlock >{{cite web |work=defensenews.com |first1=Bryant |last1=Harris |first2=Stephen |last2=Losey |first3=Megan |last3=Eckstein |url=https://www.defensenews.com/congress/2023/06/08/joint-chiefs-vacancies-loom-amid-tubervilles-senate-standoff/ |date=June 8, 2023 |title=Joint chiefs vacancies loom amid Tuberville's Senate standoff }}</ref><ref name= myers >{{cite web |first=Meghann |last=Myers |url=https://www.militarytimes.com/news/your-military/2022/09/14/dod-attempts-to-get-its-head-around-how-the-end-of-roe-affects-troops/ |date=September 14, 2022 |title=DoD attempts to get its head around how the end of Roe affects troops }}</ref> and over 200 general officer and flag officer nominations.<ref name= taylor >{{cite web |first=Daniel |last=Taylor |work=1819news |url=https://1819news.com/news/item/tuberville-blocks-senate-democrats-ninth-attempt-to-break-his-hold-on-military-promotions |date=June 16, 2023 |title=Tuberville blocks Senate Democrats' ninth attempt to break his hold on military promotions |access-date=June 18, 2023 |archive-date=June 18, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230618144248/https://1819news.com/news/item/tuberville-blocks-senate-democrats-ninth-attempt-to-break-his-hold-on-military-promotions |url-status=live }}</ref> On June 20, 2023, the Pentagon noted there are 64 three- and four-star nominations pending, with about 650 general and flag officers that will require Senate confirmation before the end of the year.<ref name= singh20Jun23 >{{cite web |first=Sabrina |last=Singh |url=https://www.war.gov/News/Transcripts/Transcript/Article/3433535/deputy-pentagon-press-secretary-sabrina-singh-holds-a-press-briefing/ |date=June 20, 2023 |title=Deputy Pentagon Press Secretary Sabrina Singh Holds a Press Briefing |access-date=December 8, 2025 |archive-date=December 10, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251210212800/https://www.war.gov/News/Transcripts/Transcript/Article/3433535/deputy-pentagon-press-secretary-sabrina-singh-holds-a-press-briefing/ |url-status=live }}</ref>}}

On July 11, Tuberville blocked the confirmation of a new [[Commandant of the United States Marine Corps|Marine Corps commandant]], leaving the Corps without a leader for the first time in two centuries.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kenney |first=Caitlin M. |date=2023-07-11 |title=Senator blocks Marine confirmation, leaving Corps with an acting commandant |url=https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2023/07/marines-without-confirmed-commandant-after-sen-tuberville-objects-motion/388356/ |access-date=2023-07-11 |website=Defense One |language=en}}</ref> By August, more than 300 generals, admirals, and policy officials had not yet been confirmed.<ref name= aug23 /> The hold also blocked the appointment of a new [[Chief of Staff of the United States Army|Army chief of staff]], vacant as of August 3, and a new [[Chief of Naval Operations|chief of naval operations]], vacant as of August 14.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/04/tuberville-hold-as-james-mcconville-retires-00109833 |title=Army chief retires as Tuberville hold snarls the Pentagon's top ranks |last=McCleary |first=Paul |website=[[Politico]] |date=August 4, 2023 |access-date=August 6, 2023 |archive-date=August 6, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230806210702/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/08/04/tuberville-hold-as-james-mcconville-retires-00109833 |url-status=live }}</ref> Five military commands at [[Redstone Arsenal]] in Alabama were also affected.<ref name="huntsvilleAffected">{{Cite web |last=Roop |first=Lee |date=2023-08-12 |title=Tuberville promotion freeze hits Redstone Arsenal |url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/08/tubervilles-military-holds-impact-redstone-arsenal-in-huntsville.html |access-date=2023-09-21 |website=al |language=en}}</ref>

On September 20, the Senate, working around Tuberville's hold in a rarely used procedure, voted to confirm three of the highest-ranking officers: the [[Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff|Joint Chiefs chairman]], Marine Corps commandant, and Army chief of staff.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Weaver |first=Al |date=2023-09-21 |title=Senate works around Tuberville to confirm three top military officials |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4216691-senate-works-around-tuberville-to-confirm-three-top-military-officials/ |access-date=2023-09-24 |website=The Hill |language=en-US |archive-date=September 21, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230921190041/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4216691-senate-works-around-tuberville-to-confirm-three-top-military-officials/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The move elevated Marine Corps general [[Eric Smith (general)|Eric Smith]] to commandant, but the hold prevented him from appointing a deputy commandant, a situation he called "not sustainable".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Loewenson |first=Irene |date=2023-09-18 |title=As both the No. 1 and No. 2 Marine, his schedule is 'not sustainable' |url=https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2023/09/18/as-both-the-no-1-and-no-2-marine-his-schedule-is-not-sustainable/ |access-date=2023-11-02 |website=Marine Corps Times |language=en |archive-date=November 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102201228/https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2023/09/18/as-both-the-no-1-and-no-2-marine-his-schedule-is-not-sustainable/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On October 29, Smith was hospitalized after suffering a heart attack. Lacking a deputy commandant or other available four-star general, the Marine Corps tapped a [[lieutenant general]] to temporarily perform the duties of commandant.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Loewenson |first=Irene |date=2023-11-01 |title=Top Marine general in stable condition after apparent heart attack |url=https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2023/11/01/top-marine-general-in-stable-condition-after-apparent-heart-attack/ |access-date=2023-11-02 |website=Marine Corps Times |language=en |archive-date=November 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102201228/https://www.marinecorpstimes.com/news/your-marine-corps/2023/11/01/top-marine-general-in-stable-condition-after-apparent-heart-attack/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On November 1, incensed senators brought dozens of military nominations to the floor; Tuberville blocked them all.<ref>{{Cite web |first1=Mary Clare |last1=Jalonick |first2=Lolita |last2=Baldor |date=2023-11-01 |title=Republicans confront Tuberville over military holds in extraordinary showdown on Senate floor |url=https://apnews.com/article/tuberville-holds-military-schumer-nominations-99a156198d325a329a98208785ea80f9 |access-date=2023-11-02 |website=Associated Press |language=en |archive-date=November 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102201227/https://apnews.com/article/tuberville-holds-military-schumer-nominations-99a156198d325a329a98208785ea80f9 |url-status=live }}</ref> The next day, the Senate confirmed a new chief of naval operations, a new Air Force chief of staff, and a new assistant commandant of the Marine Corps<ref name=":5">{{Cite web |date=2023-11-02 |title=Senate confirms first woman to lead Navy, key joint staff vacancies |first=Lauren C. |last=Williams |url=https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2023/11/senate-confirms-first-woman-lead-navy-key-joint-staff-vacancies/391753/ |access-date=2023-11-03 |website=Defense One |language=en |archive-date=November 3, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103012817/https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2023/11/senate-confirms-first-woman-lead-navy-key-joint-staff-vacancies/391753/ |url-status=live }}</ref> through a laborious process of circulating a [[cloture]] petition.<ref>{{Cite web |last=O'Brien |first=Connor |date=2023-11-02 |title=Senate confirms top Navy, Air Force picks as Tuberville feud intensifies |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/11/02/senate-navy-tuberville-franchetti-00125011 |access-date=2023-11-03 |website=[[Politico]] |language=en |archive-date=November 3, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103012817/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/11/02/senate-navy-tuberville-franchetti-00125011 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On December 5, 2023, Tuberville largely lifted his hold, which had blocked 451 promotions during the previous week; the Senate responded by promoting 425 military officers.<ref name=Decker>{{Cite news |last=Decker |first=Audrey |date=December 5, 2023 |title=Hundreds of promotions approved after Tuberville drops hold |work=Defense One |url=https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2023/12/tuberville-drops-hold-most-military-promotions/392485/}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Freking |first1=Kevin |title=Senate approves hundreds of military promotions after Republican senator ends blockade of nominees |url=https://apnews.com/article/tuberville-senate-military-holds-b4d4fe19bada70a085208c9d82c35cb5 |access-date=December 6, 2023 |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=December 6, 2023 |archive-date=December 5, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231205213150/https://apnews.com/article/tuberville-senate-military-holds-b4d4fe19bada70a085208c9d82c35cb5 |url-status=live }}</ref> But he retained his hold on 11 officers nominated for four-star positions.<ref name=Decker/> On December 19, he lifted the hold on the final 11 officers, ending the matter.<ref name="politico_1219">{{Cite web |date=December 19, 2023 |title=Senate confirms top military nominees, ending Tuberville's hold over promotions |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/12/19/senate-confirms-top-military-nominees-ending-tubervilles-hold-over-promotions-00132588 |website=POLITICO |access-date=December 20, 2023 |archive-date=December 20, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231220032036/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/12/19/senate-confirms-top-military-nominees-ending-tubervilles-hold-over-promotions-00132588 |url-status=live }}</ref>

==== Gaza ====
In 2025, Tuberville praised Trump's proposal to have the U.S. take over the [[Gaza Strip]], calling it "a good idea".<ref>{{cite news |last=Bolton |first=Alexander |date=February 6, 2025 |title=Trump's Gaza plans fall flat with GOP lawmakers |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5129173-trump-gaza-proposal-reaction/ |work=The Hill |access-date=February 6, 2025 |archive-date=February 7, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250207045821/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/5129173-trump-gaza-proposal-reaction/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==== Comments on white nationalists ====
On May 10, 2023, Birmingham-area radio station [[WBHM]] broadcast an interview in which Tuberville was asked whether he believed [[White nationalism|white nationalists]] should be allowed to serve in the [[United States military|military]]. Tuberville said the Biden administration "call[s] them that. I call them Americans." Later that day, his congressional staff released a statement that said Tuberville "was being skeptical of the notion that there are white nationalists in the military, not that he believes they should be in the military."<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://apnews.com/article/tommy-tuberville-white-nationalists-military-3a38da5a664b911260ea994415016600 |title=Sen. Tuberville criticized for remarks on white nationalists: 'I call them Americans' |last=Kinnard |first=Meg |work=[[Associated Press]] |date=May 11, 2023 |access-date=June 2, 2023 |archive-date=June 2, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230602142926/https://apnews.com/article/tommy-tuberville-white-nationalists-military-3a38da5a664b911260ea994415016600 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="Politico1">{{cite web|url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/05/10/tuberville-office-white-nationalist-comments-00096324 |title=Tommy Tuberville's office clarifies his white nationalist comments |last=Garrity |first=Kelly |website=[[Politico]] |date=May 10, 2023 |access-date=May 10, 2023 |language=en}}</ref> U.S. military leaders have said extremism in the ranks is growing.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vergun |first=David |date=February 8, 2021 |title=DOD Leaders Will Address Extremism in the Ranks |url=https://www.war.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/2497216/dod-leaders-will-address-extremism-in-the-ranks/ |access-date=May 11, 2023 |website=U.S. Department of Defense |language=en-US}}</ref> For example, an October 2020 Pentagon report said there were "white supremacist inroads in the U.S. military".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/05/tuberville-on-white-nationalists-in-the-military-i-call-them-americans.html|title=Tuberville on white nationalists in the military: 'I call them Americans'|last=Gattis|first=Paul|work=AL.com|date=May 10, 2023|access-date=June 2, 2023|archive-date=June 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230602142926/https://www.al.com/news/2023/05/tuberville-on-white-nationalists-in-the-military-i-call-them-americans.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Much independent reporting indicates this as well.<ref>{{Cite web |date=November 17, 2020 |title=Confronting the U.S. Military's White Nationalist Problem |url=https://www.usni.org/magazines/proceedings/2020/november/confronting-us-militarys-white-nationalist-problem |access-date=May 11, 2023 |website=U.S. Naval Institute |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=April 27, 2021 |title=We've Been Here Before: Learning From the Military's History with White Nationalism |url=https://warontherocks.com/2021/04/weve-been-here-before-learning-from-the-militarys-history-with-white-nationalism/ |first1=Simone |last1=Askew |first2=Jack |last2=Lowe |first3=Nette |last3=Monaus |first4=Kirsten L. |last4=Cooper |access-date=May 11, 2023 |website=War on the Rocks |language=en-US |archive-date=May 18, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210518002136/https://warontherocks.com/2021/04/weve-been-here-before-learning-from-the-militarys-history-with-white-nationalism/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

After the interview, Tuberville's brother Charles said he felt "compelled to distance himself" from Tuberville and his "ignorant, hateful rants" and "vile rhetoric".<ref name="brother">{{cite news |last1=Feinberg |first1=Andrew |title=Alabama senator condemned by his own brother for 'ignorant, hateful rants' |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/tommy-tuberville-brother-racism-b2349653.html |access-date=July 11, 2023 |work=The Independent |date=June 1, 2023}}</ref>

In July 2023, [[CNN]]'s [[Kaitlan Collins]] asked Tuberville about his earlier comments on white nationalists, whom she defined as "someone who believes that the white race is superior to other races". Tuberville called that an "opinion". He then denied white nationalists are inherently racist.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Koplowitz |first1=Howard |title=Tuberville responds to Kaitlan Collins on white nationalists being racist: 'That's your opinion' |url=https://www.al.com/politics/2023/07/tuberville-responds-to-kaitlan-collins-on-white-nationalists-being-racist-thats-some-peoples-opinion.html |access-date=July 15, 2023 |work=[[The Birmingham News|AL.com]] |publisher=Advance Local Media LLC |date=July 10, 2023 |archive-date=July 14, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230714190743/https://www.al.com/politics/2023/07/tuberville-responds-to-kaitlan-collins-on-white-nationalists-being-racist-thats-some-peoples-opinion.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Tuberville's refusal to accept the definition of a white nationalist drew heavy criticism from Democrats and Republican senators.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Turner |first1=Trish |last2=Carlson |first2=Adam |last3=Pecorin |first3=Allison |title=Tommy Tuberville reverses his claim that white nationalists are unfairly labeled racist |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/tommy-tuberville-triples-claim-white-nationalists-unfairly-labeled/story?id=101095697 |access-date=July 15, 2023 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |date=July 11, 2023 |archive-date=July 15, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230715082249/https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/tommy-tuberville-triples-claim-white-nationalists-unfairly-labeled/story?id=101095697 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Bolton |first1=Alexander |last2=Weaver |first2=Al |title=Tuberville's white nationalism comments trigger GOP uproar |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4091794-tubervilles-white-nationalism-comments-trigger-gop-uproar/ |access-date=July 15, 2023 |work=[[The Hill (website)|The Hill]] |publisher=Nexstar Media Inc. |date=July 11, 2023 |archive-date=July 15, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230715235920/https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4091794-tubervilles-white-nationalism-comments-trigger-gop-uproar/ |url-status=live }}</ref> A day later, Tuberville reversed his statement, saying, "White nationalists are racists."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Kochi |first1=Sudiksha |title='New meaning to the word idiot': Tommy Tuberville faces backlash over comments on white nationalism |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2023/07/13/tommy-tuberville-white-nationalism-racism/70408946007/ |access-date=July 15, 2023 |work=[[USA Today]] |date=July 13, 2023}}</ref>

In June 2025, during a podcast appearance with [[Benny Johnson (columnist)|Benny Johnson]], Tuberville railed against "inner-city rats" he said are "living off the American taxpayers" and advocated that President Trump defund U.S. cities governed by Democrats. He also claimed that [[The Great Replacement]] is happening.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.al.com/politics/2025/06/tuberville-says-inner-city-rats-live-off-the-american-taxpayers-trump-should-send-them-back-home.html|title=Tuberville says 'inner city rats' live off the American taxpayers: Trump should send them 'back home'|last=Thornton|first=William|publisher=[[Alabama.com]]|quote=Again, these inner-city rats, they live off the federal government. And that's one reason we're $37 trillion in debt. "And it's time we find these rats and we send them back home, that are living off the American taxpayers, that are working very hard every week to pay taxes."|date=June 26, 2025|accessdate=June 29, 2025}}</ref>

====Threats against Tuberville====
In June 2023, a New Hampshire resident was arrested and charged with threatening to assault, kidnap or murder a member of Congress.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/03/new-hampshire-man-charged-death-threat-us-senator|title=New Hampshire man arrested and charged with death threat to US senator|last=Yang|first=Maya|work=The Guardian|date=June 3, 2023|access-date=October 10, 2023}}</ref> The charging documents did not name Tuberville as the target, but did say the charge was connected to his 2023 hold on military promotions.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/new-hampshire-man-charged-threatening-kill-senator-rcna87544|title=New Hampshire man is charged with threatening to kill a senator|last=Richards|first=Zoe|work=NBC News|date=June 2, 2023|access-date=October 10, 2023|archive-date=October 11, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231011051419/https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/new-hampshire-man-charged-threatening-kill-senator-rcna87544|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.wbrc.com/2023/06/05/man-arrested-allegedly-threatening-senator-tuberville/|title=Man arrested for allegedly threatening Senator Tuberville|work=WBRC-6|date=June 5, 2023|access-date=October 10, 2023|archive-date=October 10, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010204019/https://www.wbrc.com/2023/06/05/man-arrested-allegedly-threatening-senator-tuberville/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In October 2023, [[Michael Hayden (general)|Michael Hayden]], a retired Air Force general and former [[director of the Central Intelligence Agency]], responded to a social-media post asking whether Tuberville should be removed from his committee assignments by saying, "How about the human race?" After some interpreted this as a call for Tuberville's assassination, Hayden said he was suggesting that the senator not be considered human.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/10/ex-cia-director-suggests-tuberville-be-removed-from-the-human-race-for-promotion-freeze.html |title=Ex-CIA director suggests Tuberville be removed from 'the human race' for promotion freeze |last=Roop |first=Lee |work=AL.com |date=October 10, 2023 |access-date=October 10, 2023 |archive-date=October 10, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010204003/https://www.al.com/news/2023/10/ex-cia-director-suggests-tuberville-be-removed-from-the-human-race-for-promotion-freeze.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Tuberville reported the comment to the [[United States Capitol Police]], saying that Hayden had called for his "politically motivated assassination".<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.al.com/news/2023/10/tuberville-reports-ex-cia-director-to-capitol-police-claims-michael-hayden-called-for-his-assassination.html |title=Tuberville reports ex-CIA director to Capitol Police, claims Michael Hayden called for his 'assassination' |last=Koplowitz |first=Howard |work=AL.com |date=October 10, 2023 |access-date=October 13, 2023 |archive-date=October 11, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231011091554/https://www.al.com/news/2023/10/tuberville-reports-ex-cia-director-to-capitol-police-claims-michael-hayden-called-for-his-assassination.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

On December 24, 2023, Tuberville was [[Doxing|doxxed]] and [[Swatting|swatted]], along with [[2023 swatting of American politicians|other leading activists and politicians]] in the same period.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hall |first=Mary Helene |date=2023-12-30 |title=Tommy Tuberville reportedly targeted in swatting call at Auburn home |url=https://al.com/politics/2023/12/tommy-tuberville-reportedly-targeted-in-swatting-call-at-auburn-home.html |access-date=2024-01-03 |website=al |language=en |archive-date=January 3, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240103235051/https://www.al.com/politics/2023/12/tommy-tuberville-reportedly-targeted-in-swatting-call-at-auburn-home.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

==== Department of Veterans Affairs ====
At a March 11, 2025, Committee on Veterans Affairs hearing on the mass termination of VA employees, Tuberville said that [[privatization|private companies]] with [[proprietary software|proprietary technology]] had solicited him to receive contracts to operate at the VA, and that these private companies would benefit the VA and should be strongly considered.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.veterans.senate.gov/2025/3/hearing-to-consider-pending-legislation | title=Hearing to Consider Pending Legislation | date=March 11, 2025 | access-date=March 12, 2025 | archive-date=March 11, 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250311130049/https://www.veterans.senate.gov/2025/3/hearing-to-consider-pending-legislation | url-status=live }}</ref>

